  1661	 *
  1662	 * ### Worker Layer
  1663	 * When two Workers need to reference each other (e.g. WorkerA calls
  1664	 * WorkerB and vice versa), or you simply want optimal tree-shaking,
  1665	 * define the Worker class separately from its `.make()` call. The
  1666	 * class is a lightweight identifier; `.make()` provides the runtime
  1667	 * implementation as an `export default`. Rolldown treats `.make()`
  1668	 * as pure, so any Worker that imports the class to bind it will not
  1669	 * pull in the `.make()` dependencies — the bundler tree-shakes
  1670	 * them away entirely.
  1671	 *
  1672	 * The class and `.make()` can live in the same file. This is the
  1673	 * same pattern used by `Container` and `DurableObject`,
  1674	 * and is recommended for any cross-Worker or cross-DO bindings.
